meters\n1341 |     ----------\n1342 |     X : {array-like, sparse matrix}\n1343 |         Input data.\n1344 | \n1345 |     whom : str\n1346 |         Who passed X to this function.\n1347 |     \"\"\"\n1348 |     # avoid X.min() on sparse matrix since it also sorts the indices\n1349 |     if sp.issparse(X):\n1350 |         if X.format in [\"lil\", \"dok\"]:\n1351 |             X = X.tocsr()\n1352 |         if X.data.size == 0:\n1353 |             X_min = 0\n1354 |         else:\n1355 |             X_min = X.data.min()\n1356 |     else:\n1357 |         X_min = X.min()\n1358 | \n1359 |     if X_min < 0:\n1360 |         raise ValueError(\"Negative values in data passed to %s\" % whom)\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/utils/validation.py:_generate_get_feature_names_out`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1918 | def _generate_get_feature_names_out(estimator, n_features_out, input_features=None):\n1919 |     \"\"\"Generate feature names out for estimator using the estimator name as the prefix.\n1920 | \n1921 |     The input_feature names are validated but not used. This function is useful\n1922 |     for estimators that generate their own names based on `n_features_out`, i.e. PCA.\n1923 | \n1924 |     Parameters\n1925 |     ----------\n1926 |     estimator : estimator instance\n1927 |         Estimator producing output feature names.\n1928 | \n1929 |     n_feature_out : int\n1930 |         Number of feature names out.\n1931 | \n1932 |     input_features : array-like of str or None, default=None\n1933 |         Only used to validate feature names with `estimator.feature_names_in_`.\n1934 | \n1935 |     Returns\n1936 |     -------\n1937 |     feature_names_in : ndarray of str or `None`\n1938 |         Feature names in.\n1939 |     \"\"\"\n1940 |     _check_feature_names_in(estimator, input_features, generate_names=False)\n1941 |     estimator_name = estimator.__class__.__name__.lower()\n1942 |     return np.asarray(\n1943 |         [f\"{estima