|         # Compute lof score over training samples to define offset_:\n302 |         lrd_ratios_array = (\n303 |             self._lrd[_neighbors_indices_fit_X_] / self._lrd[:, np.newaxis]\n304 |         )\n305 | \n306 |         self.negative_outlier_factor_ = -np.mean(lrd_ratios_array, axis=1)\n307 | \n308 |         if self.contamination == \"auto\":\n309 |             # inliers score around -1 (the higher, the less abnormal).\n310 |             self.offset_ = -1.5\n311 |         else:\n312 |             self.offset_ = np.percentile(\n313 |                 self.negative_outlier_factor_, 100.0 * self.contamination\n314 |             )\n315 | \n316 |         return self\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/cross_decomposition/_pls.py:PLSRegression.fit`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n634 | def fit(self, X, Y):\n635 |         \"\"\"Fit model to data.\n636 | \n637 |         Parameters\n638 |         ----------\n639 |         X : array-like of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n640 |             Training vectors, where `n_samples` is the number of samples and\n641 |             `n_features` is the number of predictors.\n642 | \n643 |         Y : array-like of shape (n_samples,) or (n_samples, n_targets)\n644 |             Target vectors, where `n_samples` is the number of samples and\n645 |             `n_targets` is the number of response variables.\n646 | \n647 |         Returns\n648 |         -------\n649 |         self : object\n650 |             Fitted model.\n651 |         \"\"\"\n652 |         super().fit(X, Y)\n653 |         # expose the fitted attributes `x_scores_` and `y_scores_`\n654 |         self.x_scores_ = self._x_scores\n655 |         self.y_scores_ = self._y_scores\n656 |         return self\n```\n\nFound file `sklearn/utils/validation.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Search `sklearn/utils/validation.py` for the full content if needed.\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"NMF\"...\n### Search Resul